AskDB — AI Data Platform
One workspace for natural-language analytics, executive dashboards, and governed data—built for business users, not SQL experts.

AI Chat
Ask questions in plain English; answers come from validated SQL on PostgreSQL, with tables, charts, SQL, and narrative—not guesses from the model alone.

Executive Intelligence
KPI cockpit, revenue trends (including clear MTD for the current month), regional performance, sunburst drill-downs, and map-style exploration for leadership reviews.

Analytics Builder
Self-service analysis without writing SQL: pick metrics, dimensions, filters, and advanced patterns (ranking, top N, moving averages, growth, contribution).

Meaning & quality
Semantic Atlas
Business glossary, measures, dimensions, and join logic in one place—so “revenue” and “region” mean the same thing in Chat, Builder, and dashboards.

Ontology Browser
Ontology Map and Relationship Network to see how makes, models, dealers, regions, and outcomes connect—stewardship and trust, not just pretty graphs.

Data Trust Center
Trust scores, dataset health, incidents, and data-quality dimensions (accuracy, completeness, timeliness, etc.) so leaders see reliability—not only charts.

Entity Catalog (Admin)
Discover new values after data loads (makes, cities, dealers) and refresh metadata so AI and analytics stay aligned with the real world.

Data access & continuity
Data Preview
Governed, paginated browsing of semantic tables with server-enforced caps—explore raw rows without exporting the warehouse to Excel.

Query History
Every question with status, SQL, trust signals, and latency; users see their own runs, admins can oversee the full audit trail.

Saved Questions
Bookmark recurring business questions for yourself or the team—reuse without retyping.

Knowledge Hub (Beta)
Upload and retrieve cited business documents to enrich context for AI answers (evolving capability—label as beta on the slide).
Governance & enterprise controls
Regional access (RBAC)
North / South / East / West users see the same app but only their zone’s data—enforced in the API and SQL path, not just hidden filters.

Admin Center & LLM governance
Configure models and limits, monitor tokens and cost estimates, refresh semantics and ontology, and review audit activity.

Hybrid AI execution
Semantic compiler and templates first, LLM when needed—with guardrails (read-only SQL, limits, validation/repair) and usage metering.

Multi-industry packs
Switch context (e.g. automotive, insurance) with YAML-driven semantic packs—one platform pattern, multiple domains.
